  "body": "Typed original call delivery now feeds the command cache before and after camera binding, and the preserving ReadPixels tail reaches the existing bridge/core. A Linux code checker validates reviewed ELF ranges against actual process mappings and bytes. The CPU collector binds actual kernel sender credentials, fresh nonce, held-child code, post-finish status, finalized stream and exit before the strict decoder accepts a receipt.\n\nThis remains inert CPU-tested infrastructure. Explicit original-address injection and reviewed profiles are caller trust boundaries; there is no live GL loader/interposer, native admission or driver-state/GPU freshness proof. Original strict0/4FAIL/Stage7INCOMPLETE remain. Current native allowance0; new native/GL/provider/model/officialORT runs0. No Cloud/registry publication or main/sharedbase merge/push.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Full1415tests:1408passed,7skipped,0failures94.349s; focused19passed1.604s.\n- 86actual CPU scenarios:48standalone plain/ASan/UBSan exact-stream/status parity,30credential/code/spool channel runs,8unsafe-allowlist installation rejections. Valid completions pass; forged/partial/extra/sink/exit/late-write cases reject.\n- One fresh whole-branch review atbcb8e11e4183b2c6f50ebd48dcad357181b77a6a found0Critical/1Important/0Minor. One RED4subcase\u2192GREEN fix rejects DSA framebuffer read-selector and GLXcontext-copy mutators as safe names. No rereview/minor polishing; all14reviewer-declined behaviors received explicit rulings. Reviewed evidence is retained in before-fix/ and Git.\n- 334indexed proofs2,202,655B are tracked in Git, including raw CPU streams/statuses/binaries, source pins, review and test logs. Build1.672748160s measures compile/link only, excluding tests/review/CI/development; native instrumentation overhead remains unmeasured.\n- All2734baseGitblobs/299oldsourcepins/10originals/main/Drafts102\u2013107/eightnative histories preserved. Changes add 349paths and modify0base/workflow files.\n\nRulings (exhaustive, including costs and every reviewer-declined behavior):\n\n1. Continue inline/samecheckout/noquestions per persistent choice \u2014 next gap is original delivery/maps/receipt binding \u2014 spends CPU/development and no native allowance.\n\n2. Explicit original-address table and bootstrap replay instead of ambient preload/dlsym or late default seeding \u2014 preserve original call counts/history before camera registration \u2014 actual resolver/loader installation remains a future qualified boundary.\n\n3. Use assembly tail routing for ReadPixels \u2014 normal C wrappers lose Panda's saved registers/returnPC \u2014 Linuxamd64-specific transport requires mapped ABI qualification before live use.\n\n4. Kernel SCMcredentials+ownedchild+proc-code/spool checks rather than trusting standalone dictionaries \u2014 bind actual CPU sender/process/bytes \u2014 this is point-in-time evidence, not hostile-root/native attestation.\n\n5. Keep actual forward counts distinct from local cache-replay applications \u2014 replay applies alreadyobserved commands through CPU no-ops \u2014 no extra original/GL call is represented as real execution.\n\n6. Compare target-file mappings around code reads, plus process starttime/executable/file identity \u2014 unrelated Python heap mappings may grow during verification \u2014 point-in-time target-code evidence only, no whole-image or future immutability claim.\n\n7. Require caller-generated fresh32Bnonce per run and isolate child environment, rather than introduce a persistent replay database or ambient loader settings \u2014 protocol binds one owned child/session; no cross-run replay registry, hostile same-UID defense, native authority or complete image attestation.\n\n8. Use one fresh whole-branch reviewer and one Important/Critical TDDfixpass; no rereview or minor polishing \u2014 sufficient independent review without repeating already-passed CPU/old-native work. Native canary/coverage/image/installation qualification remains concrete future work, not silently admitted.\n\n9. Live exports/constructor/loader/preload/resolver installation and realPanda symbol coverage stay deferred \u2014 inert address delivery is this scope \u2014 future source/runtime coverage qualification is required before native use.\n\n10. Actual Panda ABI/camera/GSG/buffer/native lifetimes stay deferred \u2014 CPU-shaped caller is the only executed provider \u2014 new native contract/identity/allocation/lifetime proof costs remain.\n\n11. Driver acceptance/GPU freshness/camera meaning/original GPU bytes remain unproven \u2014 void CPU originals supply command history only \u2014 no strict success or GPU provenance claim is gained.\n\n12. Official model/ORT/provider success/Stage7completion stay excluded \u2014 no native allowance remains \u2014 original strict0/4FAIL/Stage7INCOMPLETE are retained, with future canary cost before any expansion.\n\n13. Hostile same-UID/root modification/cryptographic attestation are outside the guarantee \u2014 owned reviewed CPUchild is the trust model \u2014 transport cannot be promoted into adversarial native attestation.\n\n14. Whole process/image/dependency/environment identity stays deferred \u2014 bounded reviewed ranges intentionally inspect selected code \u2014 future native image/environment qualification is still needed.\n\n15. Reverting-between-observation races and future code immutability are not proven \u2014 process is held cooperatively, not frozen \u2014 point-in-time observed consistency is the limit.\n\n16. Intended ABI/executed-function semantics of codeprofiles/original tables remain caller trust \u2014 byte matching cannot infer type/coverage \u2014 reviewed profile/original qualification is required for each future integration.\n\n17. Cross-run nonce uniqueness remains caller responsibility \u2014 a fresh os.urandom(32) nonce per call is required \u2014 no persistent replay database is introduced.\n\n18. Arbitrary executable sandboxing/hostile descendants/resource containment stay excluded \u2014 collector requires the reviewed CPUfixture \u2014 it must not be exposed as an arbitrary executable admission service.\n\n19. Optional NULL entry invocation/invalid string or delete spans/preinstall calls/freed storage/nonreturning originals/concurrent installation/lifecycle remain caller-precondition violations \u2014 C cannot authenticate arbitrary memory/lifetime \u2014 capable callers must satisfy bounded valid spans and serialized lifetime.\n\n20. Complete discovery of future GL mutators remains a live coveragegate \u2014 finite known unsupported classification cannot prove completeness \u2014 concrete known selector/context-copy bypasses are fixed now rather than deferred.\n\n21. Remote main/Draft/nativehistory revalidation is executor closeout work \u2014 reviewer inspected retained preservation only \u2014 executor rehashes originals and queries exact histories again before final result; no oldnative replay.\n\n22. Historical fullsuite rerun belongs to executor \u2014 reviewer independently ran newCPUmodules and inspected retained full log \u2014 one post-fix whole suite and refreshed CPUevidence supply final regression proof.\n\n23. Follow existing option2 integration choice with finishing-a-development-branch skill, preserving current checkout \u2014 user persistently authorized ownDraft/exactCI and no routine questions \u2014 no main/sharedbase merge or Cloudregistry publication; no newworktree cleanup.\n\n24. Keep exactsourceCI/assignedDraft/finalHEAD receipts external to the immutable source commit \u2014 a source file cannot contain its own finalSHA without changing it \u2014 PR body and retained output/final-verification.json close this final gate, without another CI-triggering metadata commit.\n\nDeferred minors: none.\n\nResult: docs/STAGE7_READBACK_DELIVERY_BOUNDARY_RESULT.md\nLedger: docs/STAGE7_READBACK_DELIVERY_BOUNDARY_LEDGER.md\nProofs: docs/evidence/readback-delivery-boundary-01/proof-index.json\nReview: docs/evidence/readback-delivery-boundary-01/whole-branch-review.md\nNext execution: docs/STAGE7_READBACK_DELIVERY_BOUNDARY_CONTINUATION.md\n\nStacks on feature/readback-state-suppliers-v1 atc06a3a3eb8e215a8e40054433cf4c6c4c1d42bdc. Exact immutable-source Draft/CI closeout follows below without changing the source commit.\n\nSource HEAD: 93475a36e8a68889aa632182dccd4cdc3dde39c0\n\nExact source closeout (2026-11-15T08:31:03.250926+09:00):\n\nSource93475a36e8a68889aa632182dccd4cdc3dde39c0; Draft108 remains open and unmerged; basec06a3a3eb8e215a8e40054433cf4c6c4c1d42bdc; body roundtrip verified.\n\n- pull_request: https://github.com/rownlvh8875-coder/big-model-closed-loop-benchmark/actions/runs/43653426883 \u2014 success,attempt1,2jobs,0artifacts; jobIDs 132626671301,132626671555.\n- push: https://github.com/rownlvh8875-coder/big-model-closed-loop-benchmark/actions/runs/43653415901 \u2014 success,attempt1,2jobs,0artifacts; jobIDs 132626636986,132626637234.\n\nFinal recheck: all2734baseGitblobs/299oldpins/10original artifacts match;334indexed proofs2,202,655B are inGit;349added paths and0base/workflow edits. Main48e79a7ed5aedf6daa5a62ff68d2225af7955ef1/oldDraft102\u2013107/eightnativehistories unchanged. No new native/GL/provider/officialmodel/officialORT, consumedrequest reuse, mainmerge or Cloudregistry publication. Kernel/code/stream CPU evidence does not confer live GL delivery, actual camera/lifetime/driver/GPU/native authority. Final verification: output/stage7-readback-delivery-boundary-01/final-verification.json. Next execution: docs/STAGE7_READBACK_DELIVERY_BOUNDARY_CONTINUATION.md.\n",
